    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d489">

                <pb facs="0590" n="522" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg522"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/2355¾</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">25 January, 1916</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Do you not think that it
                    would be wise to post Gerard pretty fully in this matter. I think that House
                    ought to know the full facts, but I do not like to go over Gerard’s head and
                    tell House and not him. House, according to this despatch,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d489-f1"/> will be in Berlin to-day and it is of the utmost
                    importance, of course, that he <pb facs="0591" n="523" xml:id="pg523"/> be fully
                    posted. It might be well to instruct Gerard specifically to tell House
                    everything, though I suppose he would do so in any case.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
